{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions","id":874625,"title":"I just bought Beast and I have questions!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T09:55:15-07:00","id":874625,"title":"I just bought Beast and I have questions!","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I've got my copy of Beast yesterday. I'm reading through it and I have some questions... I wouldn't mind some help with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1. I admit I don't entirely get what's the relationship between a Beast and their Horror. In one place, the rulebook says that a new Horror is created during the Devouring and it joins with a Beast. In another place, it suggests that a Beast and their Horror have always been parts of the same being, even before the Devouring... So, do the Horrors exist before their Beasts are Devoured? And is the Devouring a situation of two beings merging into one, or two halves of one being getting reunited?<br /> <br /> 2. On more practical side: what's the relationship between the Beast's Horror and their human personality? Does the human personality get completely eradicated during the Devouring? Or is a Beast, more or less, the same person as before?<br /> <br /> 3. Are there any guidelines as to what the Horrors might actually be? I mean, do they have to be human-sized? Or can a Beast transform into, say, a titanic dragon when entering their Lair?<br /> <br /> 4. From the GM perspective: what are the storytelling possibilities for Beasts? So far, I got the idea that the game could be about Beasts mixing up with other supernaturals or about fighting Heroes. But what if I don't quite like the crossover-intensive games? The &quot;fight your Hero&quot; element is a bit limited... What other stories can you tell about Beasts?<br /> <br /> 5. I was also wondering about the Beasts' motivations. What's actually motivating them to go out and investigate other supernaturals? And what motivates them to grow in power, expand their Lairs etc.?<br /> <br /> I'd be very thankful for your input <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:58:50-07:00","id":874689,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions#post874625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I admit I don't entirely get what's the relationship between a Beast and their Horror. In one place, the rulebook says that a new Horror is created during the Devouring and it joins with a Beast. In another place, it suggests that a Beast and their Horror have always been parts of the same being, even before the Devouring... So, do the Horrors exist before their Beasts are Devoured? And is the Devouring a situation of two beings merging into one, or two halves of one being getting reunited?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not the Horror was always a part of the Beast, or if it's a new thing in the person is an aspect that was muddied for the main release. When the Devouring was the Homecoming it was that the Beast was always a monster and the Homecoming was just coming into their own. This was changed with the Devouring to be less clear thus it's now a philosophical debate some Beasts engage debate about or the aspects of it. Like were they always Beasts, or is this recent; is their Horror completely new, the progeny of the Beast that handled the Devouring, is it the Beast that handled the Devouring; am I still myself, or am I just a monster wearing my body and memories as a suit etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions#post874625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. On more practical side: what's the relationship between the Beast's Horror and their human personality? Does the human personality get completely eradicated during the Devouring? Or is a Beast, more or less, the same person as before?</div> </div> </div> </div>For all practical reasons the Devouring doesn't explicitly cause any changes to the human personality beyond a nagging hunger. That being said the Begotten take to the Devouring in different ways depending on the individual. Some might need time to feel out things now that they're a Beast, others may feel more complete or confident in themselves, some might lose themselves to their new powers, and others might go into a freakout that it wasn't a dream and that they can actually feel the nightmare at the back of their mind. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions#post874625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Are there any guidelines as to what the Horrors might actually be? I mean, do they have to be human-sized? Or can a Beast transform into, say, a titanic dragon when entering their Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I mean you might consider keeping to the family theme or something when designing your Horror, but there aren't explicit rules about what can't be your Horror. (I think we generally agree that none of the existing monster splats are viable Horror material, but that's about it that I can think of.) I mean we have your classic monsters, we have your nightmare forms of real things, on this forum we've had people who came up with things like a nightmare webpage that exposes all of a person's secrets, a mirror monster, and I believe a one-eyed flying purple people eater from space. So have fun with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions#post874625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. From the GM perspective: what are the storytelling possibilities for Beasts? So far, I got the idea that the game could be about Beasts mixing up with other supernaturals or about fighting Heroes. But what if I don't quite like the crossover-intensive games? The &quot;fight your Hero&quot; element is a bit limited... What other stories can you tell about Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Building up the lair, achieving a legend to become an Incarnate, reconciling feeding your Horror with your own moral compass, the old standby of monster superheroes, heist stories, being the law, there are a few.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:49:37-07:00","id":874747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874689#post874689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not the Horror was always a part of the Beast, or if it's a new thing in the person is an aspect that was muddied for the main release. When the Devouring was the Homecoming it was that the Beast was always a monster and the Homecoming was just coming into their own. This was changed with the Devouring to be less clear thus it's now a philosophical debate some Beasts engage debate about or the aspects of it. Like were they always Beasts, or is this recent; is their Horror completely new, the progeny of the Beast that handled the Devouring, is it the Beast that handled the Devouring; am I still myself, or am I just a monster wearing my body and memories as a suit etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For all practical reasons the Devouring doesn't explicitly cause any changes to the human personality beyond a nagging hunger. That being said the Begotten take to the Devouring in different ways depending on the individual. Some might need time to feel out things now that they're a Beast, others may feel more complete or confident in themselves, some might lose themselves to their new powers, and others might go into a freakout that it wasn't a dream and that they can actually feel the nightmare at the back of their mind. </div> </div> </div>So, it's not like the Beast suddenly becomes a dragon wearing a human skin?<br /> <br /> BTW. Are there any correlations between who the person was before the Devouring and their Horror? Can I have, say, a timid young woman who has a scary Giant as her Horror?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. I mean you might consider keeping to the family theme or something when designing your Horror, but there aren't explicit rules about what can't be your Horror. (I think we generally agree that none of the existing monster splats are viable Horror material, but that's about it that I can think of.) I mean we have your classic monsters, we have your nightmare forms of real things, on this forum we've had people who came up with things like a nightmare webpage that exposes all of a person's secrets, a mirror monster, and I believe a one-eyed flying purple people eater from space. So have fun with that. </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I thought that the Horrors were supposed to be quite a lot like legendary beasts: animalistic and simple-minded?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Building up the lair, achieving a legend to become an Incarnate, reconciling feeding your Horror with your own moral compass, the old standby of monster superheroes, heist stories, being the law, there are a few. </div> </div> </div>I admit that I'm wondering how many of these can be turned into game sessions / stories? I mean, how much mileage can you take from &quot;You have a need to burn things down, what do you do?&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's the same problem I have with Promethean and Mummy: I read about these games, they seem to offer cool character types, but... I can't come up with any stories for them. Promethean seems to be about walking... walking... walking... Meanwhile, Mummy seems to be &quot;You wake up, you go for a hunt for a relic, you go to sleep, end of story&quot;. Hm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","user":"Varsovian","date":". 04-26-2016, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:05:42-07:00","id":874763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874747#post874747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit that I'm wondering how many of these can be turned into game sessions / stories? I mean, how much mileage can you take from &quot;You have a need to burn things down, what do you do?&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's the same problem I have with Promethean and Mummy: I read about these games, they seem to offer cool character types, but... I can't come up with any stories for them. Promethean seems to be about walking... walking... walking... Meanwhile, Mummy seems to be &quot;You wake up, you go for a hunt for a relic, you go to sleep, end of story&quot;. Hm...</div> </div> </div> </div>To paraphrase, drama consists of a thirsty person, a glass of water, and something between the two. You need to burn things down. What are you going to burn down? Why would you rather burn this thing down, and not that thing? What's keeping you from burning down what you want to burn down? What are the consequences of burning it down? You can get a lot of dramatic mileage out of a single feeding session.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:56:56-07:00","id":874810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874747#post874747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, it's not like the Beast suddenly becomes a dragon wearing a human skin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Begotten may think that way others don't; others will argue they were always the dragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874747#post874747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW. Are there any correlations between who the person was before the Devouring and their Horror? Can I have, say, a timid young woman who has a scary Giant as her Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd need to look for more specifics, but there was some stuff indicating that it wasn't unheard of for a Beast to have had nightmares relating to their Horror for a long time before they undergo the Devouring. As for your example, sure I mean probably not talking an anakim tyrant but that isn't ruled out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874747#post874747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I thought that the Horrors were supposed to be quite a lot like legendary beasts: animalistic and simple-minded?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Horror proper generally has one priority on it's mind. It is hungry and wants to eat. It gives no shit about whether or not the victim is innocent, deserving of what happens to it, or if the victim has learned anything from the experience. In that way Horrors can be a bit on the single minded aspect. As for legendary beasts part of what made many of the big legends dangerous was their intelligence. Bad enough to be facing a monster that's claws can rend steel like tissue paper, much worse when it knows how to handle an ambush and can manipulate the fight so that the terrain hinders its enemies. Generally speaking Beasts come from a single point, fear. To that end they are sentient nightmares whether this manifests itself as terror of a black widow the size of a bus, fracking Ancalagon the Black, Grendal, Sutr, Slenderman, the Rake, the Worm the Walks, the siren, Jormagundr, or that fucking creepy ass doll that everyone's aunt seems to have a collection of and for some god forsaken reason keep in rows and rows in the living room with the frelling motion sensitive lights that you swear you saw watching you from the doorway that one night. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's all viable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874747#post874747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit that I'm wondering how many of these can be turned into game sessions / stories? I mean, how much mileage can you take from &quot;You have a need to burn things down, what do you do?&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's the same problem I have with Promethean and Mummy: I read about these games, they seem to offer cool character types, but... I can't come up with any stories for them. Promethean seems to be about walking... walking... walking... Meanwhile, Mummy seems to be &quot;You wake up, you go for a hunt for a relic, you go to sleep, end of story&quot;. Hm...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're viewing this a bit much in the abstract I think. Yes eventually many are the actions of the Beast that eventually boil down to &quot;and then I eat,&quot; but the trick is dealing with the eating. (I haven't read Mummy or Promethean, so can't help you there.) For Beasts there's also family. Are others family because you relate to them, are they your family because of proximity, are they family because you are relates, does just being a Beast make other Beasts your kin, does being a monster make other monsters family, what the hell does being family mean, etc? Those are a major theme for Beasts to explore. <br /> <br /> Then you've got your feeding. The basic level is reconciling your morals with your desire to feed. I mean how do you reconcile trying to be a good person with the fact that your Horror (let's say a predator) really really wants to find some athletic type who can give a good chase, chase them till their heart is beating as fast as it goes before it causes a heart attack, punch your fist through their chest, rip out their still beating heart, and then devour it on the spot so they can see it as they die. Does this make you a horrible person? Does just having a part of you that wants to do this make you a horrible person?<br /> <br /> Then we get into the more advanced feeding. See at the low levels minor stuff works fine. You're a ravager you want to wreck stuff? Great throw a molitov or six at a church and see how much of a result that gets you. Nemesis? Get someone's car towed for parking in the red zone. Tyrant? Crush everyone at trivia night at the local bar with it being abundantly clear your teammates are only here because you promised them nachos. <br /> The higher satiety levels though require work. A Nemesis? Well your Horror always had a fondness for the violent crimes, but as you've gotten it more well fed it has become picky. It's turning it's nose up at the standard domestic violence and homicide cases. So you turn your attention to extreme violence, serial killers and torturers. So of course now you've had to figure out the linking element between a bunch of idiots getting drunk and getting killed wrecking their car (some with additional victims others not) and how to find the SoB who was handling the psychological torture to drive them to do this, and if you're going to turn them in to the authorities how are you going to prove they did it? A Ravager. You need a big statement, something that makes people feel unsafe or horrified. Are you going to kill someone who should be almost untouchable or at the least no one can understand why someone would kill them? Are you going to destroy something big and important to people? Will it look like the Eiffel Tower fell because a freak hurricane and lightning storm took it out, was Mt. Rushmore burned to ashes by a lone nut job or a group of nutjobs, will you destroy a city, how many people will you kill, are you trying to make a statement with your actions or do you just want to wreck stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:59:23-07:00","id":875166,"title":"","content":"Other than &quot;Beauty and the Beast&quot;, the most Beast-y text of Beast-y texts IMHO is &quot;Crimson Peak&quot;.<br /> <br /> The eye doctor is a Hero.<br /> <br /> Also, a huge part of the Beast Ready-Made PCs I wrote--they're not out yet, but soon--is different stories that you could tell focused on each of the characters, or on the group as a whole, so that might be useful re: seeing different potential Chronicles. When they come out, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T05:54:25-07:00","id":875533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions#post874625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> I've got my copy of Beast yesterday. I'm reading through it and I have some questions... I wouldn't mind some help with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1. I admit I don't entirely get what's the relationship between a Beast and their Horror. In one place, the rulebook says that a new Horror is created during the Devouring and it joins with a Beast. In another place, it suggests that a Beast and their Horror have always been parts of the same being, even before the Devouring... So, do the Horrors exist before their Beasts are Devoured? And is the Devouring a situation of two beings merging into one, or two halves of one being getting reunited?<br /> <br /> 2. On more practical side: what's the relationship between the Beast's Horror and their human personality? Does the human personality get completely eradicated during the Devouring? Or is a Beast, more or less, the same person as before?</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you familiar with the idea of goetic demons? In 1e, there was this idea that every person had the embodiment of their Vice in their head that tempted them to do things. There was also the Daimon that urged them to improve self. And your human personality was the Ego that tried to balance the two. <br /> <br /> This is my personal belief, but I feel that the Horror is your new goetic demon, that little demon on your shoulder that embodies your Id and all your base urges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Are there any guidelines as to what the Horrors might actually be? I mean, do they have to be human-sized? Or can a Beast transform into, say, a titanic dragon when entering their Lair? </div> </div> </div> Your Horror is generally shaped by what Atavisms you know. You want a giant dragon, you learn the atavisms related to size and dragon-like abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. From the GM perspective: what are the storytelling possibilities for Beasts? So far, I got the idea that the game could be about Beasts mixing up with other supernaturals or about fighting Heroes. But what if I don't quite like the crossover-intensive games? The &quot;fight your Hero&quot; element is a bit limited... What other stories can you tell about Beasts? </div> </div> </div> Beast is the Overlord / Dungeon Keeper game. You set up your Dungeon (aka Lair), you recruit minions (Kin/other supernaturals) and you fight heroes. Beast, as a game, is designed to be the &quot;crossover&quot; game. All those vamps, wolves, mages, and fae you recruit? You do that by getting involved with fighting off Huntsmen, exploring the Hisil, and devling into immortal politics. Other games are your plots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. I was also wondering about the Beasts' motivations. What's actually motivating them to go out and investigate other supernaturals? And what motivates them to grow in power, expand their Lairs etc.? </div> </div> </div> Other supernaturals are literally power for Beasts. <br /> <br /> - Using your Hunger to fill your Satiety is actually really difficult - takes an entire session for one of the brood to just get a single roll to feed. Family Dinner is a much more effective way of maintaining stable Satiety levels.<br /> - Other supernaturals allow you to learn/create Nightmares.<br /> - Observing and talking with other supernaturals about how they freak out mortals (Integrity loss) are a major justification for raising your Lair dots. <br /> <br /> The more supernatural friends you have, the stronger you are. The only thing you don't get from hanging around other supernaturals are more Atavisms; you get those from hanging out with other Beasts. <br /> <br /> In theory, you can ignore other supernaturals and do all this development on your own. However, not only is it more difficult, but it is also more fraught with danger. You attract far more heroes and encounter more dangers in the Primordial Dream that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:22:29-07:00","id":875659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=875533#post875533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is the Overlord / Dungeon Keeper game. You set up your Dungeon (aka Lair), you recruit minions (Kin/other supernaturals) and you fight heroes. Beast, as a game, is designed to be the &quot;crossover&quot; game. All those vamps, wolves, mages, and fae you recruit? You do that by getting involved with fighting off Huntsmen, exploring the Hisil, and devling into immortal politics. Other games are your plots.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a more introspective note, the sympathetic nature of Kinship means a lot of the stuff that the Begotten do reflects on their development re: what is frightening about them and how the theme of their chunk of the Temenos shakes out in nuance.<br /> <br /> Put more plainly, it's part of what &quot;exploring your Legend&quot; means as a Lair-raising method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T04:22:14-07:00","id":877549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874625-i-just-bought-beast-and-i-have-questions?p=874747#post874747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(. . . ) So, it's not like the Beast suddenly becomes a dragon wearing a human skin?<br /> <br /> BTW. Are there any correlations between who the person was before the Devouring and their Horror? Can I have, say, a timid young woman who has a scary Giant as her Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the others have pointed out, that's one of the questions the final draft raises. In the Kickstarter preview, you were always the monster, wrapped in human flesh, and the &quot;Homecoming&quot; just helped you come to terms with this fact. In the final release, its more of a philosophical question, one you can answer in your own games (if you want to).<br /> <br /> As for your example character . . . .yeah, I could see that. A proto-Beast's Horror often haunts their nightmares, long before the Devouring (still don't like that term). Your &quot;timid young woman&quot; might have become that way as a reaction to her Horror, terrified by what it was sharing with her through nightmares. Or maybe her timidity attracted the interest of a &quot;scary giant&quot; Horror. . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interesting. I thought that the Horrors were supposed to be quite a lot like legendary beasts: animalistic and simple-minded? </div> </div> </div>Whether pre-Devouring Horrors are intelligent beings is still an open question. They certainly don't <i>think</i> like humans (or have human priorities), but that doesn't mean they're mindless, after all . . .<br /> <br /> However, Post-Devouring, my read is that the bulk of the intelligence (human and Horror) goes where the Beast is. If they're on Earth, the Horror (back in the Lair) is sort of a shadow of its former self, just going through the motions. If the Beast is back in the Lair (and not completely satiated), the Horror gets the shared mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit that I'm wondering how many of these can be turned into game sessions / stories? I mean, how much mileage can you take from &quot;You have a need to burn things down, what do you do?&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Comic book characters like Batman and the Punisher make great examples of Beasts with a &quot;Hunger for Punishment&quot;. You could run a campaign where the Beast(s) try to clean up a corrupt city, feeding on everyone from gang members to corrupt politicians.<br /> <br /> Or you could go with more of a bounty hunter vibe, tracking down Nazis, international fugitives, war criminals . . . hunting the worst of the worst across the world. Not every country has an extradition treaty, after all, and some are corrupt enough that a well-connected fugitive can stall indefinitely. But the worse their crimes, the longer they stall, the better the meal they make to a Nemesis . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}